{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For the way is contrary (yarat) before me</b> — For the one walking perverted (yarat) his path and twisted it before my eyes, for I am the one who knows and testifies. Or <b>before me (lenegdi)</b> — that he perverted the way to act contrary to my will, as in the language of Onkelos (Onkelos on Numbers 22:32), like \"for they angered before the builders\" (Nehemiah 3:37). <b>Yarat</b> is a root meaning to twist/pervert, and likewise \"and by the hand of the wicked He will twist me (yirteneini)\" (Job 16:11) — He will pervert me. And the matter is as I explained (Ramban on Numbers 22:20): the going had permission from the honored HaShem, but Balaam perverted it by going with them with the intention of cursing the people:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:49.653601163Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}